# Ship round trip to Europe across four turns. Base: turns_spring_1600_events' output (France, Spring 1600, turn 108).
# Fixture: every other French map unit fortified (orders 6, so nothing wakes and asks for orders), France and England
# at peace (euro_relation 0x60 both ways, else English raids capture units), Caravel #148 (already bound for Europe)
# parked in Quebec; Caravel #121 (Tobacco 69 + Furs 39) on the high seas at (50,29), full moves, selected.
key r                      # Return to Europe from the high seas: the Caravel leaves the map for the eastbound lane
wait 3
key space                  # end turn 108 (no unit left to move)
wait 30
key Return                 # Colonization Help: Time Scale (two turns a year from now on)
wait 6
key Return                 # price of Cigars in La Rochelle rises to 11 (shown before the colony notices, #1821)
wait 6
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Quebec up to 60%: Continue turn
wait 6
key space                  # end turn 109 (Autumn 1600): the Caravel is still at sea
wait 30
key Return                 # Iroquois gift (16 Ore) at Port au Prince
wait 6
key Return                 # King raises the tax by 1% (Kiss pinky ring, row 0)
wait 6
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Port au Prince up to 12%
wait 6
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Martinique up to 51%
wait 6
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Guadeloupe up to 70%
wait 6
key Return                 # new cargo of Horses ready at Montreal (storage full)
wait 6
# Spring 1601 (turn 110): the Caravel docks in La Rochelle and the Europe screen opens on it (Loading: Caravel).
click 155 155              # the Caravel's icon in the harbor: European harbor options menu (Enter acts on the focused panel only, #1739)
wait 6
key Down
key Down                   # "Unload all cargo" (row 2)
key Return                 # sells 39 Furs (net 114) and 69 Tobacco (net 202): gold 429 -> 745
wait 6
click 299 93               # RECRUIT: three Free Colonists in the pool, passage 400 gold
wait 3
key Down                   # row 1, first Free Colonist
key Return                 # recruited: gold 745 -> 345, the colonist joins the dock, the pool slot refills
wait 6
click 155 155              # harbor options menu again (the Caravel's icon)
wait 6
key Down                   # "Set sail for the New World" (row 1)
key Return                 # "Shall we set sail" prompt
wait 6
key Return                 # Yes: the Caravel sails west, two dock colonists board it ("get on next ship"), back to the map
wait 6
key space                  # end turn 110
wait 30
key Return                 # Tupi gift (6 Tobacco) at Guadeloupe
wait 6
key Return                 # price of Cigars falls to 11
wait 6
key Return                 # price of Coats rises to 11
wait 6
key space                  # end turn 111 (Autumn 1601)
wait 30
# Spring 1602 (turn 112): the Caravel reappears at (50,29) with the two colonists aboard, selected, full moves.
